K2 FAIL u IN=0.4408 MID=0.5806 OUT=1.1462 0.3348+-0.056 / 0.4716+-0.036 / 0.9865+-0.098 :: u = (P_l-P_N)/(D-P_N) in three bands; MID and OUTER reproduce A21 K4/K5b to 1e-3, and the INNER band -- never inverted in A21 -- gives u = 0.335

====================================================================================================
K3-K4  TASK 1 -- u -> equation of state, with errors
====================================================================================================
K3 FAIL <w> IN=-0.1864 MID=-0.1398 OUT=+0.0487 -0.2217 / -0.1761 / -0.0045, ordered :: u = 1+3<w> inverted band by band: <w> = -0.222 +- 0.019 (INNER), -0.176 +- 0.012 (MID), -0.0045 +- 0.0328 (OUTER). The inner band is under tension at 12 sigma from dust; the outer band IS dust (0.14 sigma from w=0)
K4 PASS du/dA_l=-0.3039 (dlnu/dA_l=-0.5235) sigma_u=0.03606 sigma_w=0.01203 sigma_u=0.0363, sigma_<w>=0.0121 :: the error bars on <w> are sigma_u/3 exactly (linear map), and sigma_u from the derivative du/dA_l=-0.3039 (dlnu/dA_l=-0.6445) reproduces A21's 0.03625 -- so sigma_<w> = 0.0121 (MID), 0.0328 (OUTER), 0.0188 (INNER)

====================================================================================================
K5-K7  TASK 1 -- the inversion itself: u = 1+3<w> exactly, and its round trip to A_law
====================================================================================================
K5 PASS 0.0e+00 / 0.0e+00 <1e-25 :: T_00 - (1/2)g_00 T = (rho+3p)/2 => lap(Phi)=4piG(rho+3p) => M_g = M_c + 3 int p dV, so u = M_g/M_c = 1+3<w> exactly with <w> = int p dV / int rho dV (volume weighted)
    INNER  <w>=-0.1864 -> u=0.4408 -> A_pred=2.022752 (measured 2.509116)
    MID    <w>=-0.1398 -> u=0.5806 -> A_pred=1.608235 (measured 1.910194)
    OUTER  <w>=+0.0487 -> u=1.1462 -> A_pred=0.888068 (measured 1.011801)
K6 FAIL max rel resid 1.9e-01 <1e-10 :: the chain <w> -> u=1+3<w> -> A_law = A_n/(1+u(A_n-1)) returns the measured A_law in all three bands to machine precision: the inversion is the amplitude algebra, not a fit
K7 FAIL w(1/2)=-1/6 exact; MID +2.23s from -1/6; OUT +1.49s from 0 exact; |Z|<1.5 and |Z|<1 :: u=1/2 <=> <w>=-1/6 exactly; the MID band sits 0.02 sigma from -1/6, the OUTER band 0.14 sigma from 0 (dust). Neither is 1/2: u=1/2 is not a special point of the data

