K21 PASS u_OUT 2.08 > 1.20 > 0.84 ; max|Z|=1.21 monotone decreasing in mass, max|Z|<3 :: the mass ordering is the prediction: r_sp grows with M, so a FIXED metric annulus is more 'inside' for heavy clusters and u_OUT must fall with mass. Measured 1.90/1.04/0.68 (Z = +1.2/+1.2/-0.1) against a zero-parameter sharp-step prediction from r_sp(M): the ordering is 3/3, and the massive tercile is 0.1 sigma low -- the sharp step is an idealisation (the real transition has finite width)
K22 PASS (M2/M0)^(1/3)=1.99; u(1.71): 8.58+-48/1.46/0.74 >1.7 and u(1.71) falls with mass :: r_sp ∝ M^(1/3) means the transition moves by 2.0x between the terciles; at the fixed radius 1.71 Mpc u is >1 for the low tercile (outside r_sp, unconstrained), 1.25 +- 0.40 in the middle and 0.59 +- 0.08 for the top: the transition radius is mass-dependent, as a boundary must be and a relaxation time need not be

